==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|conceptioun|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|fro}} {{term|conception|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|conceptio||a comprehending, a collection, composition, an expression, also a becoming pregnant|lang=la}}, from {{term|concipere}}, past participle {{term|conceptus||conceive}}; see [[conceive]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/kənˈsɛpʃən/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/k@n"sEpS@n/}}
* {{audio|En-us-conception.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The act of [[conceive|conceiving]].
# The state of being conceived; the [[beginning]].
# The [[fertilization]] of an [[ovum]] by a [[sperm]] to form a [[zygote]].
# The start of [[pregnancy]].
# The formation of a [[conceptus]] or an [[implanted]] [[embryo]].
# The power or [[faculty]] of [[apprehend]]ing of forming an [[idea]] in the mind; the power of recalling a past sensation or perception; the ability to form [[mental]] [[abstraction]]s.
# An [[image]], idea, or [[notion]] formed in the mind; a [[concept]], [[plan]] or [[design]].

====Quotations====

* {{RQ:Authorized Version}}, Genesis 3:16
*: Unto the woman he said, I will greatly multiply thy sorrow and thy '''conception'''; in sorrow thou shalt bring forth children; and thy desire shall be to thy husband, and he shall rule over thee.

====Antonyms====
* [[misconception]]

====Related terms====
* [[conceive]]
* [[concept]]

